From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-Id: <20260904-istoreos-brcmfmac-ap-station-signal-fix@local>
From: istoreos-nanopi-m4b <local@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: report station signal in AP/Master mode

In brcmf_cfg80211_get_station() the per-station RSSI is filled from
sta_info_le.rssi[] first; if those entries are all zero (which is what
the firmware returns in AP/Master mode for BCM43456 and similar
chips), the function falls through to a fallback that issues
BRCMF_C_GET_RSSI to read the connected peer's signal.

That fallback is gated by BRCMF_VIF_STATUS_CONNECTED, which is only
set when the local interface is operating as a STA and is associated
to an AP.  In AP/Master mode (hostapd) this bit is never set, so the
fallback never runs and NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL is never reported.

A second issue: BRCMF_C_GET_RSSI in AP mode requires the peer MAC in
scb_val.ea, otherwise the firmware returns 0.

The visible effect on NanoPi-M4B with the BCM43456 (AP6256) running
iStoreOS-24.10 is that the LuCI "Associated Stations" view shows
"--- dBm" for every connected client, even though the link is healthy.

Fix:
  * allow the BRCMF_C_GET_RSSI fallback to also run in AP/Master
    mode, gated by brcmf_is_apmode(ifp->vif);
  * populate scb_val.ea with the requested station's MAC in the AP
    path so the firmware returns the right peer's RSSI.

The STA path is unchanged in behavior: in STA mode, scb_val.ea stays
zero (the firmware ignores it and returns the connected AP's RSSI),
and the new OR condition is a no-op because brcmf_is_apmode() is
false there.

Signed-off-by: istoreos-nanopi-m4b <local@local>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c    | 14 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -3211,11 +3211,21 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_get_station(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev,
 			sinfo->signal = total_rssi / count_rssi;
 			sinfo->signal_avg = total_rssi_avg / count_rssi;
 		} else if (test_bit(BRCMF_VIF_STATUS_CONNECTED,
-			&ifp->vif->sme_state)) {
-			memset(&scb_val, 0, sizeof(scb_val));
+				    &ifp->vif->sme_state) ||
+			   brcmf_is_apmode(ifp->vif)) {
+			memset(&scb_val, 0, sizeof(scb_val));
+			/* In AP/Master mode, BRCMF_C_GET_RSSI requires the
+			 * peer MAC in scb_val.ea; without it, the firmware
+			 * returns 0 and the signal stays unfilled.  In STA
+			 * mode the firmware returns the connected AP's RSSI
+			 * regardless of ea, so leaving ea zero is harmless
+			 * there and we only set it in the AP path.
+			 */
+			if (brcmf_is_apmode(ifp->vif))
+				memcpy(scb_val.ea, mac, ETH_ALEN);
 			err = brcmf_fil_cmd_data_get(ifp, BRCMF_C_GET_RSSI,
 						     &scb_val, sizeof(scb_val));
 			if (err) {
 				bphy_err(drvr, "Could not get rssi (%d)\n",
 					 err);
 				goto done;
-- 
